	"identifying_description": "Leaf of vellum with opaque watercolor, gold paint, and gold paper trim with scene of two young people in English garden, flying tethered birds. \"R.G.\" monogram on reverse. Sticks and guards of carved and incised ivory that may show scene from story of Achilles. Glass jewel and copper alloy rivet.",
	"web_text": "This fan's leaf features a young couple flying tethered birds, possibly doves, while a shepherdess looks on. The “R.G.” monogram on this fan's reverse, seen in the image below, suggests that the fan was commissioned for a wedding. Fans with illustrations of wedding themes were often given to brides-to-be as tokens of affection from their fiancées, or by brides to their attendants.",
	"didactic_label": "This fan's leaf features a young couple flying tethered birds, possibly doves, while a shepherdess looks on. The “R.G.” monogram on this fan's reverse, seen in the image below, suggests that the fan was commissioned for a wedding. Fans with illustrations of wedding themes were often given to brides-to-be as tokens of affection from their fiancées, or by brides to their attendants.",
	"exhibition_history_text": "Fans of the Eighteenth Century, Textiles Education Gallery, de Young Museum, 9/25/18 - 7/7/19\nGallery 9C, Legion of Honor, 2000\nMidwinter Fair Centenary, 1994\nFans in Fashion, Legion of Honor, 5/23/81 - 8/30/81",
